**THE CORPUS COLUMN AND THE PER-CELL COLUMNS ARE AN ORDER OF MAGNITUDE APART, AND THAT IS A FACT ABOUT THE CELL SET, NOT ABOUT THE OBSERVER.** IN WALK MODE (fix1 -- this explanation is WALK-ONLY, and the sentence round 1 wrote was unscoped) two cells -- `f7_n1000_path_warm` and `f7_n800_path_warm` -- carry 95.9551 % of the U0 set's instructions between them (1.08e12 and 6.66e11 against 1.82e12 for all 27) and both take the same TWO major iterations as every other cell, so their attached ratio is ~1.00004 and they pull the SUM-of-medians corpus figure onto themselves. THE SAME TWO CELLS CARRY ONLY 6.8034 % IN ssn AND 8.7003 % IN ipm, where the corpus and per-cell columns are correspondingly close together. The per-cell median is the figure to read for what an attached observer costs a typical cell; the corpus figure is the one the FLAT definition names, and both are inside the band in all three modes.

Counter check: **PASS -- byte-identical**.
